course: dictionary
lesson: 11257
title: Woven: made by crossing threads
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something was made. Woven is one of them. When you weave, you pass threads, strips or stems over and under each other, one after another, until they hold together as one piece. «Kente is a bright woven cloth from Ghana.» Woven tells you that the cloth was made by crossing threads, not printed or painted.
explain: Read the words around woven to check. Cloth, basket and mat are things that can be made by weaving. A web is woven by a spider, so the word tells you how it was made. Ask yourself: how was this thing made? If the answer is by crossing threads or strips, woven fits.
explain: Woven can also describe ideas and stories. When a story is woven from many tales, the tales are joined together closely, like threads in a cloth. «Kente» is a Ghanaian cloth that is bright and famous, so it helps to picture the threads when you read.
fact: Woven means made by crossing threads, strips or stems over and under each other.
fact: Woven is the past participle of weave, so you may also see weave and weaving.
fact: «Kente» is a bright woven cloth from Ghana.
fact: Woven baskets and woven mats are made from strips or stems crossed over each other.
fact: When used about stories or ideas, woven means joined together closely, as in a story woven from many tales.
exercise: «Kente is a bright woven cloth from Ghana.» What does woven mean here? | Painted with bright colours | *Made by crossing threads over and under each other | Sewn from one single piece | Bought in a shop
exercise: «The story is woven from many old tales.» What does woven mean in this sentence? | Written in a hurry | Sung loudly | *Joined together closely, like threads in a cloth | Torn into small pieces
exercise: Which of these is most likely to be woven? | A paper plate | A glass jar | *A wicker basket made from crossed stems | A metal spoon
test: «The spider has woven a web across the gate.» What has the spider made? | A hole in the ground | A nest for its eggs | *A web made by crossing threads | A cave in the wall
test: Which clue in «The mat was woven from reeds» tells you how the mat was made? | *The word woven, which means made by crossing reeds | The word mat | The word from | The word was
exam: «Kente is a bright woven cloth from Ghana.» Using the clues in the sentence, what does woven mean? | Cut out from paper | *Made by crossing threads over and under each other, so the cloth was made by weaving | Painted onto cloth with a brush | Made by crossing threads over and under each other
